## Summary table (server surfaces)

| # | Server surface | Primary file(s) | Enforcement mechanism |
|---|----------------|-----------------|------------------------|
| 1 | Connect/gRPC MemoService | `memo_service.go`, `memo_service_comments.go`, `memo_relation_service.go`, `memo_service_converter.go` | Query filters, RPC gates, relation filters |
| 2 | Connect/gRPC ReactionService | `reaction_service.go` | Inline visibility checks per handler |
| 3 | Connect/gRPC AttachmentService | `attachment_service.go` | `checkAttachmentAccess` at RPC boundary |
| 4 | Connect/gRPC memo attachments | `memo_attachment_service.go` | Inline check in `ListMemoAttachments` |
| 5 | Connect/gRPC UserService stats | `user_service_stats.go` | Visibility-constrained memo queries |
| 6 | Connect/gRPC UserService notifications | `user_service_notifications.go` | Payload redaction via `canViewerAccessMemo` |
| 7 | HTTP file server | `fileserver/fileserver.go` | HTTP 401/403 before serving attachment bytes |
| 8 | HTTP RSS | `rss/rss.go` | Public-only memo queries |
| 9 | HTTP sitemap | `frontend/frontend.go` | Public-only memo queries |
| 10 | SSE push | `sse_hub.go` | Per-client event filtering |
| 11 | Email outbound | `notification/email.go` | Skip email if receiver can't view memo |

---

## Explicitly excluded (not view-enforcement sites)

- **Helper definitions only:** `checkMemoReadAccess` (`memo_service.go:39–68`), `checkAttachmentAccess` (`attachment_service.go:422–454`), `checkAttachmentPermission` (`fileserver.go:650–703`), `canViewerAccessMemo` (`user_service_notifications.go:302–316`, `email.go:306–319`), `canReceive` (`sse_hub.go:134–143`) — these implement policy but enforcement happens at the call sites above.
- **Client-side filtering:** `web/` — not server enforcement.
- **Method-level auth only:** `authz.go` / `acl_config.go` — authentication and public-RPC allowlists, not memo visibility.
- **Share-token bypass:** `memo_share_service.go` `GetMemoByShare` — alternate access path via share token, not standard visibility enforcement.
- **Write-side mention filtering:** `memo_mention_helpers.go` — controls who gets mention inbox items, not memo read authorization on existing data.

